-- title:
--   Rigidity of constants in a Drinfeld chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) with maximal ideal generated by an element $\pi_1$, and suppose every element $x$ of the residue field of $W_1$ satisfies $x^{q^n} = x$ for some $n \ge 1$. Let $W_2$ be a second complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_2$, and assume $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_2$. Let $f_2, u_2, v_2$ be formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W_2$ with $u_2$ and $v_2$ units, and suppose $f_2 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lies in the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$. Put $S_2 = W_2[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\pi_2)v_2 - f_2u_2)$, where $C$ denotes the constant-series map. Then for every ring homomorphism $\theta : W_1 \to S_2$ with $\theta(\pi_1)$ equal to the class of $C(\pi_2)$, there is a ring homomorphism $\rho : W_1 \to W_2$ with $\rho(\pi_1) = \pi_2$ such that $\theta(w)$ is the class of $C(\rho(w))$ for all $w \in W_1$.
--
--   The statement expresses a rigidity property of the constants in a Drinfeld local chart: any map of a complete discrete valuation ring with residue field algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_q$ into the chart ring that sends a uniformiser to the chart's uniformiser factors through the constants $W_2 \hookrightarrow S_2$, so it is induced by a map $W_1 \to W_2$ of coefficient rings. It is used in the comparison of two Drinfeld charts of one completed stalk on a modular curve at full level, where it transports data between the charts by producing the coefficient-ring homomorphism $\rho$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_exists_ringHom_forall_apply_eq_mk_C_of_apply_eq_mk_C_of_forall_pow_pow_eq.lean

